---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Sample Trade Review" description="A real Private Trade Review, published with the trader's permission: a profitable options record whose profit came from two days.">
<main class="page">
  <header class="head">
    <div class="eyebrow">Sample review · Case 001 · Index options · 185 trades · 38 trading days · Aug–Oct 2026</div>
    <h1>Up ₹2.01 lakh. Two days made it; <em>the other 36 lost money.</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">A real review, published with the trader's written permission. Names, accounts and instruments are removed, and the five strategies are renamed A to E. Every figure is computed from the trader's own export.</p>
    <p class="consent">Like every review, this one describes the record. It doesn't recommend any trade, strategy or position size.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="kpis" aria-label="Headline numbers">
    <div class="kpi"><span>Net P&amp;L, after charges</span><b class="gain">₹2,01,141</b></div>
    <div class="kpi"><span>Charges paid</span><b>₹15,712</b></div>
    <div class="kpi"><span>Win rate · profit factor</span><b>49.2% · 1.59</b></div>
    <div class="kpi"><span>Deepest drawdown</span><b class="leak">₹90,668</b></div>
    <div class="kpi"><span>Losing days</span><b>23 of 38</b></div>
    <div class="kpi"><span>Strategies</span><b>5</b></div>
  </section>

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="f1">
    <span class="tag">Finding 1 · Concentration</span>
    <h2 id="f1">Two days made ₹2,94,646. The other 36 lost ₹93,505.</h2>
    <div class="chart">
      <svg id="daily" viewBox="0 0 760 220" role="img" aria-label="Net P&amp;L for each of 38 trading days. Most days are small losses; 15 September (+₹1,83,393) and 8 October (+₹1,11,253) tower over the rest."></svg>
    </div>
    <div class="legend"><span><i style="background:var(--gain)"></i>Day up</span><span><i style="background:var(--leak)"></i>Day down</span></div>
    <p>The account was down <b>₹53,222</b> on 10 September, a month and a half in. It went from there to its final result on two days: <b>15 September</b> (+₹1,83,393) and <b>8 October</b> (+₹1,11,253). Without those two days, the record is a <b>loss of ₹93,505</b> over 36 days.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="f2">
    <span class="tag">Finding 2 · Where the profit came from</span>
    <h2 id="f2">₹1,43,854 came from two positions the system's own log calls "orphaned".</h2>
    <p>On 15 September, two Strategy A positions were closed by the end-of-day safety sweep, which closes positions the system is no longer managing. They made <b>₹83,094</b> and <b>₹60,760</b>. That is <b>71.5%</b> of the account's net profit, from 2 of 185 trades, neither closed by the strategy's own exit rules.</p>
    <div class="rows">
      <div class="row"><span>Strategy A, all 45 trades</span><span class="num gain">+₹1,48,713</span></div>
      <div class="row"><span>Strategy A, 4 safety-sweep exits ("orphaned position")</span><span class="num gain">+₹1,45,841</span></div>
      <div class="row"><span>Strategy A, the other 41 trades</span><span class="num">+₹2,872</span></div>
      <div class="row"><span>Strategy A, 26 stop-loss exits</span><span class="num leak">−₹1,90,151</span></div>
      <div class="row"><span>Whole account without the two orphaned positions</span><span class="num">+₹57,287 on 183 trades</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="f3">
    <span class="tag">Finding 3 · Strategy by strategy</span>
    <h2 id="f3">Two strategies earned the money. Three lost it back.</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Strategy</th><th class="num">Trades</th><th class="num">Win rate</th><th class="num">Net</th><th class="num">Charges</th><th class="num">Profit factor</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>A · opening-range options</td><td class="num">45</td><td class="num">35.6%</td><td class="num gain">+₹1,48,713</td><td class="num">₹5,134</td><td class="num">1.70</td></tr>
          <tr><td>B · target-based options</td><td class="num">22</td><td class="num">86.4%</td><td class="num gain">+₹69,792</td><td class="num">₹3,648</td><td class="num">5.08</td></tr>
          <tr><td>C · hedged strangle</td><td class="num">50</td><td class="num">56.0%</td><td class="num leak">−₹2,998</td><td class="num">₹2,913</td><td class="num">0.82</td></tr>
          <tr><td>D · iron condor</td><td class="num">60</td><td class="num">45.0%</td><td class="num leak">−₹10,616</td><td class="num">₹3,572</td><td class="num">0.89</td></tr>
          <tr><td>E · EMA trend</td><td class="num">8</td><td class="num">12.5%</td><td class="num leak">−₹3,750</td><td class="num">₹445</td><td class="num">0.01</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>A and B together: <b>+₹2,18,505</b> on 67 trades, with a deepest drawdown of ₹79,612. C, D and E together: <b>−₹17,364</b> on 118 trades. Charges cost more than C's trades lost before charges (C was −₹85 gross), and a third of D's loss is charges. D's four legs are each charged as a separate trade.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="f4">
    <span class="tag">Finding 4 · Time of day</span>
    <h2 id="f4">Trades opened before 11:00 made ₹2,30,143. Trades opened 11:00–14:00 lost ₹65,177.</h2>
    <div id="hours" aria-label="Net P&amp;L by entry hour"></div>
    <p>Late-morning and midday entries were 89 of the 185 trades, almost half the record, and lost money as a group in every hour. The four afternoon trades are too few to read anything into.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="f5">
    <span class="tag">Finding 5 · Exits</span>
    <h2 id="f5">Targets closed 9 trades out of 185.</h2>
    <p>Every trade had a planned target, but stops, breakeven stops, time exits, square-offs and D's regime-shift rule closed the rest. D and E never reached a target. D's regime-shift exits (36 trades) cost <b>₹14,697</b>, more than D lost in total.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="f6">
    <span class="tag">Finding 6 · Measured in R</span>
    <h2 id="f6">Only one strategy's edge stays positive across its whole likely range.</h2>
    <p>This system used trailing stops only, so there was no fixed planned risk per trade. Here <b>1R is each strategy's own average loss</b>, a standard substitute (Van Tharp) when stops aren't fixed. The 90% range comes from 10,000 bootstrap resamples of the strategy's own trades. SQN is shown only where a strategy has 30 or more trades.</p>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Strategy</th><th class="num">1R</th><th class="num">Expectancy</th><th class="num">90% range</th><th class="num">SQN</th><th class="num">Losses past 2R</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>A · opening-range options</td><td class="num">₹7,289</td><td class="num">+0.45R</td><td class="num">−0.20 to +1.18R</td><td class="num">1.04</td><td class="num">1 · −₹17,274</td></tr>
          <tr><td>B · target-based options</td><td class="num">₹5,704</td><td class="num gain">+0.56R</td><td class="num gain">+0.17 to +0.98R</td><td class="num">— (22 trades)</td><td class="num">0</td></tr>
          <tr><td>C · hedged strangle</td><td class="num">₹746</td><td class="num leak">−0.08R</td><td class="num">−0.34 to +0.18R</td><td class="num">−0.50</td><td class="num">3 · −₹5,368</td></tr>
          <tr><td>D · iron condor</td><td class="num">₹2,798</td><td class="num leak">−0.06R</td><td class="num">−0.38 to +0.23R</td><td class="num">−0.34</td><td class="num leak">5 · −₹51,579</td></tr>
          <tr><td>E · EMA trend</td><td class="num">₹541</td><td class="num leak">−0.87R</td><td class="num">−1.25 to −0.49R</td><td class="num">— (8 trades)</td><td class="num">0</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Strategy A made <b>+20.4R</b> in total, and its four orphaned-position exits were <b>+20.0R</b> of that. Its best single trade was +11.4R. D's five losses past 2R cost more than D lost overall. Measuring 1R by average loss hides stops that were ignored, because the average absorbs them, so we count the losses past 2R separately. Every strategy here also has fewer than the 100 trades our rule asks for, so read these figures as direction, not proof.</p>
    <p class="note">An earlier draft of this review used the stop stored in the export as 1R. That stop had already been trailed past entry on 85 trades, which made its R figures wrong.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="sum" class="head">
    <h2 id="sum">What the record shows</h2>
    <ul class="summary">
      <li>The net profit is real, but it rests on two days and on two positions the system was no longer managing.</li>
      <li>Two strategies made more than the whole account. The other three were net losers, and part of their loss was charges.</li>
      <li>Results split by time of day: early entries made the money, late-morning and midday entries lost it.</li>
      <li>Planned targets rarely decided the exit. Measured in R, only Strategy B's edge stays positive across its likely range. Strategy A's R total is almost entirely its orphaned-position exits.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="lede">Doubling the size of a record like this doubles its pattern too: the same two-day dependence, the same midday losses, the same ₹90,668 drawdown, twice as large.</p>
    <div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/">See how a review works</a></div>
  </section>

  <footer>Case 001 · published with the trader's permission · computed from the trader's broker-side P&amp;L export (185 closed trades, 3 Aug–8 Oct 2026). Gross ₹2,16,853, charges ₹15,712, net ₹2,01,141. This describes past trades. It isn't investment advice or research, and it doesn't indicate future results. We aren't registered with SEBI as an investment adviser or research analyst.</footer>
</main>
</Base>

<style is:global>
/* Layout: one reading column of ruled sheets, the same tokens as the landing page; each finding is a sheet with its number first. */
:root {
  --canvas: #f6f6f4; --sheet: #ffffff; --ink: #141414; --muted: #6b6b68; --rule: #e4e4e0;
  --accent: #2b45d9; --accent-soft: #e8ecff; --leak: #c2410c; --leak-soft: #fdebe2; --gain: #3f7d52;
  --font-display: "Instrument Serif", "Iowan Old Style", Georgia, serif;
  --font-body: "Geist", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
  --font-mono: "Geist Mono", ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
  --radius: 14px;
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root:not([data-theme="light"]) {
    --canvas: #111211; --sheet: #191a19; --ink: #ededea; --muted: #9a9a95; --rule: #2a2b29;
    --accent: #8197ff; --accent-soft: #1d2340; --leak: #f08a5d; --leak-soft: #3a2117; --gain: #7cc191;
    color-scheme: dark;
  }
}
:root[data-theme="dark"] {
  --canvas: #111211; --sheet: #191a19; --ink: #ededea; --muted: #9a9a95; --rule: #2a2b29;
  --accent: #8197ff; --accent-soft: #1d2340; --leak: #f08a5d; --leak-soft: #3a2117; --gain: #7cc191;
  color-scheme: dark;
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
body { margin: 0; background: var(--canvas); color: var(--ink); font: 400 1rem/1.6 var(--font-body); -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }
.page { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; padding: clamp(40px, 7vw, 88px) max(16px, env(safe-area-inset-right, 0px)) 72px max(16px, env(safe-area-inset-left, 0px)); display: grid; gap: 28px; }
.eyebrow { font: 500 0.8125rem/1.4 var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }
h1 { margin: 0; font: 400 clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 3.9rem)/1 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -.02em; text-wrap: balance; }
h1 em { font-style: italic; color: var(--leak); }
h2 { margin: 0; font: 400 clamp(1.6rem, 3.6vw, 2.1rem)/1.1 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -.01em; text-wrap: balance; }
p { margin: 0; }
.lede { font-size: 1.1875rem; color: var(--muted); max-width: 58ch; text-wrap: pretty; }
.head { display: grid; gap: 16px; }
.consent { font: 400 0.8125rem/1.5 var(--font-mono); color: var(--muted); padding: 10px 14px; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 10px; background: var(--sheet); }
.mono, .num { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.leak { color: var(--leak); } .gain { color: var(--gain); }

.kpis { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1px; background: var(--rule); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: var(--radius); overflow: hidden; }
@media (max-width: 600px) { .kpis { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
.kpi { background: var(--sheet); padding: 16px; display: grid; gap: 2px; min-width: 0; }
.kpi span { font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--muted); }
.kpi b { font: 400 1.6rem/1.2 var(--font-display); }

.card { background: var(--sheet); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: clamp(18px, 3.5vw, 28px); display: grid; gap: 14px; min-width: 0; }
.card .tag { font: 500 11px var(--font-mono); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; color: var(--accent); }
.card p { color: var(--muted); }
.card p b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 500; }
.big { font: 400 clamp(1.8rem, 4.5vw, 2.4rem)/1.1 var(--font-display); }
.chart svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
.chart .axis { fill: var(--muted); font: 400 10px var(--font-mono); }
.legend { display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; font: 400 12px var(--font-mono); color: var(--muted); }
.legend i { display: inline-block; width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 2px; margin-right: 6px; vertical-align: -1px; }

.table-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.875rem; }
th, td { text-align: left; padding: 9px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); white-space: nowrap; }
th { font: 500 11px var(--font-mono); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em; color: var(--muted); }
td.num, th.num { text-align: right; }
tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }

.rows { display: grid; }
.row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto; gap: 12px; padding: 9px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); font-size: 0.875rem; }
.row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
.bar-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 112px minmax(0, 1fr) 96px; gap: 10px; align-items: center; font-size: 0.8125rem; padding: 5px 0; }
.bar-row .track { height: 10px; position: relative; }
.bar-row .track i { position: absolute; top: 0; height: 100%; border-radius: 3px; }
.bar-row .track::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 50%; top: -3px; bottom: -3px; border-left: 1px dashed var(--muted); }
@media (max-width: 520px) { .bar-row { grid-template-columns: 92px minmax(0, 1fr) 84px; } }

.coverage-bar { display: flex; height: 8px; border-radius: 99px; overflow: hidden; background: var(--rule); }
.coverage-bar i { display: block; }
.note { font: 400 0.8125rem/1.55 var(--font-mono); color: var(--muted); }
.summary { border-top: 1px solid var(--ink); display: grid; }
.summary li { list-style: none; padding: 14px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
.summary ul { margin: 0; padding: 0; }
.cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; align-items: center; }
.btn { display: inline-flex; padding: 11px 18px; border-radius: 999px; font: 500 0.8125rem/1 var(--font-body); text-decoration: none; border: 1px solid var(--ink); background: var(--ink); color: var(--canvas); }
footer { font: 400 11px/1.6 var(--font-mono); color: var(--muted); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: 20px; }
a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 3px; border-radius: 6px; }
</style>

<script>
  const DAILY = [["2026-08-03",-7888],["2026-08-04",41707],["2026-08-05",-12780],["2026-08-06",9498],["2026-08-07",-1645],["2026-08-10",608],["2026-08-11",-14097],["2026-08-12",-1217],["2026-08-17",-16333],["2026-08-18",-4614],["2026-08-19",-8040],["2026-08-20",5353],["2026-08-21",-1283],["2026-08-24",-2132],["2026-08-25",-4032],["2026-08-26",6454],["2026-08-27",301],["2026-09-01",-5971],["2026-09-02",-7701],["2026-09-03",-12860],["2026-09-04",962],["2026-09-08",-4000],["2026-09-09",-13766],["2026-09-10",255],["2026-09-15",183393],["2026-09-17",-24327],["2026-09-18",-1697],["2026-09-21",-3444],["2026-09-22",21550],["2026-09-23",-5268],["2026-09-24",7925],["2026-09-28",3331],["2026-09-29",747],["2026-09-30",-7720],["2026-10-01",10042],["2026-10-05",-4095],["2026-10-07",-37326],["2026-10-08",111253]];
  const HOURS = [["09:15–09:59",62,160481],["10:00–10:59",30,69662],["11:00–11:59",48,-33240],["12:00–12:59",24,-17412],["13:00–13:59",17,-14525],["14:00–15:30",4,36176]];
  const SVG_NS = "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg";
  const RUPEES = new Intl.NumberFormat("en-IN");

  function svgElement(tag, attributes) {
    const element = document.createElementNS(SVG_NS, tag);
    Object.entries(attributes).forEach(([name, value]) => element.setAttribute(name, value));
    return element;
  }

  function signedRupees(value) {
    return (value < 0 ? "−₹" : "+₹") + RUPEES.format(Math.abs(value));
  }

  function drawDailyChart() {
    const svg = document.getElementById("daily");
    const chart = { left: 8, right: 752, top: 22, bottom: 196 };
    const highest = Math.max(...DAILY.map(([, net]) => net));
    const lowest = Math.min(...DAILY.map(([, net]) => net));
    const y = (value) => chart.top + (highest - value) / (highest - lowest) * (chart.bottom - chart.top);
    const slot = (chart.right - chart.left) / DAILY.length;
    svg.appendChild(svgElement("line", { x1: chart.left, x2: chart.right, y1: y(0), y2: y(0), stroke: "var(--muted)", "stroke-dasharray": "2 3" }));
    DAILY.forEach(([date, net], index) => {
      const top = Math.min(y(net), y(0));
      const bar = svgElement("rect", { x: chart.left + index * slot + slot * 0.18, y: top, width: slot * 0.64, height: Math.max(Math.abs(y(net) - y(0)), 1), rx: 1.5, fill: net >= 0 ? "var(--gain)" : "var(--leak)" });
      const tip = svgElement("title", {});
      tip.textContent = `${date}: ${signedRupees(net)}`;
      bar.appendChild(tip);
      svg.appendChild(bar);
      if (net > 100000) {
        const label = svgElement("text", { x: chart.left + index * slot + slot / 2, y: top - 6, "text-anchor": "middle", class: "axis" });
        label.textContent = `${date.slice(8)} ${date.slice(5, 7) === "09" ? "Sep" : "Oct"}`;
        svg.appendChild(label);
      }
    });
    const start = svgElement("text", { x: chart.left, y: 214, class: "axis" });
    start.textContent = "3 Aug";
    const end = svgElement("text", { x: chart.right, y: 214, class: "axis", "text-anchor": "end" });
    end.textContent = "8 Oct";
    svg.append(start, end);
  }

  function drawHours() {
    const root = document.getElementById("hours");
    const largest = Math.max(...HOURS.map(([, , net]) => Math.abs(net)));
    HOURS.forEach(([label, trades, net]) => {
      const width = Math.abs(net) / largest * 50;
      const row = document.createElement("div");
      row.className = "bar-row";
      row.innerHTML = `<span class="mono">${label}</span><span class="track"><i style="left:${net >= 0 ? 50 : 50 - width}%;width:${width}%;background:${net >= 0 ? "var(--gain)" : "var(--leak)"}"></i></span><span class="num ${net >= 0 ? "gain" : "leak"}" style="text-align:right">${signedRupees(net)}</span>`;
      row.title = `${trades} trades`;
      root.appendChild(row);
    });
  }

  drawDailyChart();
  drawHours();
</script>
